{"answer":"To add a new output format to Sphinx you create a new subclass of the abstract base class in sphinx.builders (e.g. in sphinx/builders/your_new.py).  Your class must implement all required methods – build, get_outdated_docs, get_target_uri, prepare_documents, build_finished, etc. – as specified in sphinx/builders/base.py.  Once the class is defined you register it in the builder registry (the mapping in sphinx/builders/__init__.py).  After the builder is registered you can invoke it with ...``bash
sphinx-build -b your_new /src /out
``.  This is how the Sphinx Builder API can be extended for new output formats."}

